/S /P
/P 812 0 R
/ActualText (Nearly 69% of the API services we scanned had issues related to Unrestricted Resource Consumption, making them susceptible to Denial of Service \(DoS\) attacks.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 813 0 R
/ActualText (Approximately 11.1% of the services experienced issues associated with Security Misconfiguration. Improper customization and configuration options in GraphQL can create security gaps if not properly managed.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Exposed secrets: More than 4,000 exposed secrets have been uncovered in GraphQL API responses, including access tokens, passwords, and credit card numbers. Preventing public access to these details is crucial.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (GraphQL-specificity remains a general concern: 13.4% of the vulnerabilities found are specific to the GraphQL language and its frameworks - showing that organizations do not correctly manage the new risks associated with the technology yet. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
